@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `msig-cgl-nouns`
IMPORT `msig-cgl-record`

-- DEFINITIONS (src:52-175). Each defined term is one rule here, in the order the policy
-- defines them, with the definition quoted above it. "insured" and "named insured" are
-- roles, carried by `A person claimed against` (nouns) and decided by Persons Insured in
-- each coverage part; their entries here are comments.
--
-- Dates: the policy period is read INCLUSIVE of both of its stated days (NOTES.md, fork
-- F1). The date a harm "occurs" is passed in as a parameter so that the Claim Series
-- Clause (src:768) can substitute its deemed date (msig-cgl-answer.l4).

§ `DEFINITIONS`
-- src:52 | DEFINITIONS
-- src:54 | When used in this Policy (including endorsements forming a part hereof):

§§ `"automobile"`

-- src:56 | "automobile" means a land motor vehicle, trailer or semi-trailer designed for travel on public roads (including any
-- src:57 | machinery or apparatus attached thereto), but does not include mobile equipment;
@ref src:56-57
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vehicle is an automobile` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is a land motor vehicle, trailer or semi-trailer designed for travel on public roads`
    AND NOT `the vehicle is mobile equipment` claim

§§ `"bodily injury" and "property damage"`

-- "bodily injury ... sustained by any person which occurs during the policy period,
-- including death at any time resulting therefrom": the injury is dated, and a death
-- that follows it counts whenever it happens.
-- src:59 | "bodily injury" means bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by any person which occurs during the policy period,
-- src:60 | including death at any time resulting therefrom;
-- "property damage": (1) physical injury to or destruction of tangible property during
-- the period, with its loss of use whenever; (2) loss of use of uninjured property,
-- dated by the OCCURRENCE that causes it.
-- src:164 | "property damage" means (1) physical injury to or destruction of tangible property which occurs during the policy period,
-- src:165 | including the loss of use thereof at any time resulting therefrom, or (2) loss of use of tangible property which has not been
-- src:166 | physically injured or destroyed provided such loss of use is caused by an occurrence during the policy period;
@ref src:59-60, 164-166
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      d      IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` d MEANS
    `the day` d `falls from` (policy's `the policy period begins`) `to` (policy's `the policy period ends`) `inclusive`

-- The date each kind of harm is dated by, before any deeming by the Claim Series Clause.
@ref src:59, 164, 166
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the harm is dated by` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the harm`
    WHEN `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`
        THEN claim's `the date of the occurrence`
    OTHERWISE claim's `the date the injury occurs`

@ref src:59-60
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm is bodily injury` claim MEANS
    claim's `the harm` EQUALS `bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by a person`

@ref src:164-166
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm is property damage` claim MEANS
        claim's `the harm` EQUALS `physical injury to or destruction of tangible property`
    OR  claim's `the harm` EQUALS `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`

@ref src:59-60, 164-166
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
      d      IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm is bodily injury or property damage as defined` policy claim d MEANS
        (   `the harm is bodily injury` claim
         OR `the harm is property damage` claim)
    AND `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` d

§§ `"collapse hazard"`

-- src:62 | "collapse hazard" includes "structural property damage" as defined herein and property damage to any other property at
-- src:63 | any time resulting therefrom. "Structural property damage" means the collapse of or structural injury to any building or
-- src:64 | structure due to (1) grading of land, excavating, borrowing, filling, back-filling, tunnelling, pile driving, cofferdam work or
-- src:65 | caisson work or (2) moving, shoring, underpinning, raising or demolition of any building or structure or removal or rebuilding
-- src:66 | of any structural support thereof. The collapse hazard does not include property damage (1) arising out of operations
-- src:69 | Page 1 of 14
-- src:71 | Revised General Liability Policy Form
-- src:72 | performed for the named insured by independent contractors, or (2) included within the completed operations hazard or the
-- src:73 | underground property damage hazard, or (3) for which liability is assumed by the insured under an incidental contract;
@ref src:62-73
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property damage is included within the collapse hazard` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage is the collapse of or structural injury to a building or structure, or results at any time from such collapse or injury`
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the collapse or structural injury is due to grading of land, excavating, borrowing, filling, back-filling, tunnelling, pile driving, cofferdam work or caisson work`
         OR "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the collapse or structural injury is due to moving, shoring, underpinning, raising or demolition of a building or structure, or removal or rebuilding of its structural support`)
    AND NOT "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors`
    AND NOT "(2)" ... (   `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
                       OR `the property damage is included within the underground property damage hazard` claim)
    AND NOT "(3)" ... `the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim

§§ `"completed operations hazard"`

-- src:74 | "completed operations hazard" includes bodily injury and property damage arising out of operations or reliance upon a
-- src:75 | representation or warranty made at any time with respect thereto, but only if the bodily injury or property damage occurs after
-- src:76 | such operations have been completed or abandoned and occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named
-- src:77 | insured. "Operations" include materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection therewith. Operations shall be deemed
-- src:78 | completed at the earliest of the following times:
-- src:80 | (1) when all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured under the contract have been completed,
-- src:82 | (2) when all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured at the site of the operations have been
-- src:83 | completed or
-- src:85 | (3) when the portion of the work out of which the injury or damage arises has been put to its intended use by any person or
-- src:86 | organization other than another contractor or subcontractor engaged in performing operations for a principal as a part
-- src:87 | of the same project.
-- src:89 | Operations which may require further service or maintenance work, or correction, repair or replacement because of any
-- src:90 | defect or deficiency, but which are otherwise complete, shall be deemed completed.
@ref src:77-90
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the operations are deemed completed or abandoned` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured under the contract had been completed when the harm occurred`
    ..  "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured at the site had been completed when the harm occurred`
    ..  "(3)" ... `for` claim `,` `the portion of the work out of which the harm arises had been put to its intended use, when the harm occurred, by a person or organization other than another contractor or subcontractor engaged in performing operations for a principal as part of the same project`
    ..  "or abandoned" ... `for` claim `,` `the operations had been abandoned when the harm occurred`
    OR  "otherwise complete" ... `for` claim `,` `the operations were otherwise complete when the harm occurred, though they might require further service or maintenance work, or correction, repair or replacement because of a defect or deficiency`

-- src:92 | The completed operations hazard does not include bodily injury or property damage arising out of
-- src:94 | (a) operations in connection with the transportation of property, unless the bodily injury or property damage arises out of a
-- src:95 | condition in or on a vehicle created by the loading or unloading thereof,
-- src:97 | (b) the existence of tools, uninstalled equipment or abandoned or unused materials, or
-- src:99 | (c) operations for which the classification stated in the Policy or in the Company's manual specifies "including completed
-- src:100 | operations";
@ref src:92-100
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the completed operations hazard does not include it` claim MEANS
        "(a)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of operations in connection with the transportation of property`
                   AND NOT `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of a condition in or on a vehicle created by its loading or unloading`)
    ..  "(b)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the existence of tools, uninstalled equipment or abandoned or unused materials`
    OR  "(c)" ... `for` claim `,` `the classification stated in the Policy or in the Company's manual for the operations specifies including completed operations`

@ref src:74-100
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim MEANS
        (   `the harm is bodily injury` claim
         OR `the harm is property damage` claim)
    AND `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of operations, including materials, parts or equipment furnished with them, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`
    AND `the operations are deemed completed or abandoned` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the harm occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured`
    AND NOT `the completed operations hazard does not include it` claim

§§ `"elevator"`

-- src:102 | "elevator" means any hoisting or lowering device to connect floors or landings whether or not in service, and all appliances
-- src:103 | thereof including any car, platform, shaft, hoistway, stairway, runway, power equipment and machinery; but does not include
-- src:104 | an automobile servicing hoist, or a hoist without a platform outside a building if without mechanical power or if not attached to
-- src:105 | building walls, or a hod or material hoist used in alteration, construction or demolition operations, or an inclined conveyor
-- src:106 | used exclusively for carrying property or a dumbwaiter used exclusively for carrying property and having a compartment
-- src:107 | height not exceeding four feet:
@ref src:102-107
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the device is an elevator` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the device is a hoisting or lowering device to connect floors or landings`
    AND NOT (    `for` claim `,` `the device is an automobile servicing hoist`
             OR  `for` claim `,` `the device is a hoist without a platform outside a building, without mechanical power or not attached to building walls`
             OR  `for` claim `,` `the device is a hod or material hoist used in alteration, construction or demolition operations`
             OR  `for` claim `,` `the device is an inclined conveyor used exclusively for carrying property`
             OR  `for` claim `,` `the device is a dumbwaiter used exclusively for carrying property and having a compartment height not exceeding four feet`)

§§ `"explosion hazard"`

-- src:109 | "explosion hazard" includes property damage arising out of blasting or explosion. The explosion hazard does not include
-- src:110 | property damage (1) arising out of the explosion of air or steam vessels, piping under pressure, prime movers, machinery or
-- src:111 | power transmitting equipment, or (2) arising out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors,
-- src:112 | or (3) included within the completed operations hazard or the underground property damage hazard, or (4) for which liability
-- src:113 | is assumed by the insured under an incidental contract;
@ref src:109-113
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property damage is included within the explosion hazard` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of blasting or explosion`
    AND NOT "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of the explosion of air or steam vessels, piping under pressure, prime movers, machinery or power transmitting equipment`
    AND NOT "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors`
    AND NOT "(3)" ... (   `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
                       OR `the property damage is included within the underground property damage hazard` claim)
    AND NOT "(4)" ... `the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim

§§ `"incidental contract"`

-- src:115 | "incidental contract" means any written (1) lease of premises, (2) easement agreement, except in connection with
-- src:116 | construction or demolition operations on or adjacent to a railroad, (3) undertaking to indemnify a municipality required by
-- src:117 | municipal ordinance, except in connection with work for the municipality, (4) sidetrack agreement or (5) elevator maintenance
-- src:118 | agreement;
@ref src:115-118
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`that contract or agreement is an incidental contract` claim MEANS
        "any written" ... `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is in writing`
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is a lease of premises`
         OR "(2)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is an easement agreement`
                       AND NOT `for` claim `,` `that easement agreement is in connection with construction or demolition operations on or adjacent to a railroad`)
         OR "(3)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is an undertaking to indemnify a municipality required by municipal ordinance`
                       AND NOT `for` claim `,` `that undertaking is in connection with work for the municipality`)
         OR "(4)" ... `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is a sidetrack agreement`
         OR "(5)" ... `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is an elevator maintenance agreement`)

@ref src:73, 113, 175, 342
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured assumed liability for the harm under a contract or agreement`
    AND `that contract or agreement is an incidental contract` claim

§§ `"insured"`

-- A role, not a test of its own: whoever Persons Insured of the applicable coverage part
-- makes an insured (msig-cgl-part-cgl.l4, msig-cgl-part-pco.l4). The second sentence
-- (each insured separately, but one set of limits) is why a claim record is one claim
-- against one insured, while the limits are applied to the occurrence as a whole.
-- src:120 | "insured" means any person or organization qualifying as an insured in the "Persons Insured" provision of the applicable
-- src:121 | insurance coverage. The insurance afforded applies separately to each insured against whom claim is made or suit is
-- src:122 | brought, except with respect to the limits of the Company's liability;

§§ `"mobile equipment"`

-- src:124 | "mobile equipment" means a land vehicle (including any machinery or apparatus attached thereto), whether or not
-- src:125 | self-propelled, (1) not subject to motor vehicle registration, or (2) maintained for use exclusively on premises owned by or
-- src:126 | rented to the named insured, including the ways immediately adjoining, or (3) designed for use principally off public roads, or
-- src:127 | (4) designed or maintained for the sole purpose of affording mobility to equipment of the following types forming an integral
-- src:128 | part of or permanently attached to such vehicle; power cranes, shovels, loaders, diggers and drills; concrete mixers (other than
-- src:129 | the mix-in-transit type); graders, scrapers, rollers and other road construction or repair equipment; air-compressors, pumps
-- src:130 | and generators, including spraying, welding and building cleaning equipment; and geophysical exploration and well
-- src:131 | servicing equipment;
@ref src:124-131
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vehicle is mobile equipment` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is a land vehicle`
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is not subject to motor vehicle registration`
         OR "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is maintained for use exclusively on premises owned by or rented to the named insured, including the ways immediately adjoining`
         OR "(3)" ... `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is designed for use principally off public roads`
         OR "(4)" ... `for` claim `,` `the vehicle is designed or maintained for the sole purpose of affording mobility to equipment of a type the definition of mobile equipment lists, forming an integral part of it or permanently attached to it`)

§§ `"named insured" and "named insured products"`

-- "named insured": the person or organization named in Item 1 of the declarations. A
-- role: `the named insured` in `A person claimed against`.
-- src:133 | "named insured" means the person or organization named in Item 1, of the declarations of this Policy;
-- "named insured products": the definition's own exclusion (a vending machine or other
-- property rented or located for use of others but not sold) is read with the products
-- hazard below. The definition defines "named insured products" and then speaks of
-- "named insured's products"; the two are read as one term (NOTES.md, fork F3).
-- src:135 | "named insured products" means goods or products manufactured, sold, handled or distributed by the named insured or
-- src:136 | by others trading under his name, including any container thereof (other than a vehicle), but "named insured's products" shall
-- src:137 | not include a vending machine or any property other than such container, rented to or located for use of others but not sold;
@ref src:135-137
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm arises out of the named insured's products` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the named insured's products, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`
    AND NOT `for` claim `,` `those products are a vending machine, or other property apart from a container, rented to or located for use of others but not sold`

§§ `"occurrence"`

-- src:139 | "occurrence" means an accident, including continuous repeated exposure to conditions, which results in bodily injury or
-- src:140 | property damage neither expected nor intended from the standpoint of the insured:
@ref src:139-140
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm was caused by an occurrence` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm results from an accident, including continuous or repeated exposure to conditions`
    AND NOT `for` claim `,` `the harm was expected or intended from the standpoint of the insured`

-- All three limits clauses deem harm from continuous or repeated exposure to substantially
-- the same general conditions to arise out of ONE occurrence (src:542-544, 685-687,
-- 812-814). The caller labels each harm's occurrence and, where there is one, its
-- general conditions of exposure; two harms count as one occurrence if either label
-- matches.
-- src:542 | Coverage A and B - For the purpose of determining the limit of the Company's liability, all bodily injury and property
-- src:543 | damage arising out of continuous or repeated exposure to substantially the same general conditions shall be considered as
-- src:544 | arising out of one occurrence.
@ref src:542-544, 685-687, 812-814
GIVEN one   IS A `A claim against an insured`
      other IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harms of` one `and of` other `count as one occurrence for the limits` MEANS
        one's `the occurrence` EQUALS other's `the occurrence`
    OR  `the same general conditions of exposure` (one's `the general conditions of exposure`) (other's `the general conditions of exposure`)
    WHERE
        `the same general conditions of exposure` x y MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST a  THEN
                CONSIDER y
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST b  THEN a EQUALS b

§§ `"policy territory"`

-- The proviso at src:156-157 stands at the left margin after limb (3), so it is read as
-- qualifying all three limbs; and it bites only where a suit has been brought (NOTES.md,
-- fork F2).
-- src:142 | "policy territory" means:
-- src:144 | (1) any nation or area described in the Policy, or
-- src:150 | (2) international waters or air space, provided the bodily injury or property damage does not occur in the course of travel
-- src:151 | or transportation to or from any other nation or area, or
-- src:153 | (3) anywhere in the world with respect to damages because of bodily injury or property damage arising out of a product
-- src:154 | which was sold for use or consumption within the territory described in the Policy,
-- src:156 | provided the original suit for such damages is brought subject to the provisions of the Jurisdiction clause as stipulated in the
-- src:157 | Policy;
@ref src:142-155
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm occurs in a place the policy territory names` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm occurs within a nation or area described in the Policy`
    ..  "(2)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the harm occurs in international waters or air space`
                   AND NOT `for` claim `,` `the harm occurs in the course of travel or transportation to or from another nation or area`)
    OR  "(3)" ... `for` claim `,` `the damages arise out of a product sold for use or consumption within the territory described in the Policy`

@ref src:156-157
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the original suit is brought subject to the Jurisdiction clause` claim MEANS
        NOT `for` claim `,` `a suit for the damages has been brought`
    OR  `for` claim `,` `the original suit for the damages was brought in a court of competent jurisdiction within Vietnam`

@ref src:142-157
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim MEANS
        `the harm occurs in a place the policy territory names` claim
    AND "provided" ... `the original suit is brought subject to the Jurisdiction clause` claim

§§ `"products hazard"`

-- src:159 | "products hazard" includes bodily injury and property damage arising out of the named insured's products or reliance
-- src:160 | upon a representation or warranty made at any time with respect thereto, but only if the bodily injury or property damage
-- src:161 | occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured and after physical possession of such products has
-- src:162 | been relinquished to others;
@ref src:159-162
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the harm is included within the products hazard` claim MEANS
        (   `the harm is bodily injury` claim
         OR `the harm is property damage` claim)
    AND `the harm arises out of the named insured's products` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the harm occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured`
    AND `for` claim `,` `physical possession of those products had been relinquished to others when the harm occurred`

§§ `"underground property damage hazard"`

-- src:168 | "underground property damage hazard" includes underground property damage as defined herein and property damage
-- src:169 | to any other property at any time resulting therefrom, "Underground property damage" means property damage to wires,
-- src:170 | conduits, pipes, mains, sewers, tanks, tunnels, any similar property, and any apparatus in connection therewith, beneath the
-- src:171 | surface of the ground or water, caused by and occurring during the use of mechanical equipment for the purpose of grading
-- src:172 | land, paving, excavating, drilling, borrowing, filling, back-filling or pile driving. The underground property damage hazard does
-- src:173 | not include property damage (1) arising out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors, or
-- src:174 | (2) included within the completed operations hazards, or (3) for which liability is assumed by the insured under an incidental
-- src:175 | contract.
@ref src:168-175
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property damage is included within the underground property damage hazard` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage is to wires, conduits, pipes, mains, sewers, tanks, tunnels, similar property or apparatus connected with them, beneath the surface of the ground or water, or results at any time from such damage`
    AND `for` claim `,` `that underground damage was caused by and occurred during the use of mechanical equipment for grading land, paving, excavating, drilling, borrowing, filling, back-filling or pile driving`
    AND NOT "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors`
    AND NOT "(2)" ... `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
    AND NOT "(3)" ... `the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim
